---
import DocsLayout from "@layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Git Integration" description="Git support in Axon">
    <h1>Git Integration</h1>

    <p>
        Axon includes built-in Git support for version control workflows. You
        can view changes, inspect diffs, browse history, work with graph
        context, manage branches, stashes, worktrees, conflicts, and draft
        commit messages without leaving the editor.
    </p>

    <figure>
        <img src="/media/screenshots/axon-screenshot-02.png" alt="Axon source control panel with changed files and inline diff markers" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Git status belongs close to the files and editor so changed files, diffs, and line-level markers stay connected to the work you are doing.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>File Tree Git Status</h2>
    <p>The file tree shows Git status with colored labels:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><span class="text-axon-green">Green</span> — Modified</li>
        <li><span class="text-axon-red">Red</span> — Deleted</li>
        <li><span class="text-axon-cyan">Blue</span> — Untracked</li>
        <li><span class="text-axon-muted">Gray</span> — Ignored (hidden)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Gutter Markers</h2>
    <p>In the editor, gutter markers show line-level changes:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><span class="text-axon-green">Green bar</span> — Added line</li>
        <li><span class="text-axon-red">Red bar</span> — Removed line</li>
        <li><span class="text-axon-cyan">Blue bar</span> — Modified line</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Source Control Panel</h2>
    <p>
        Open the Source Control panel from the sidebar to access Git operations:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>View all changed files</li>
        <li>Stage / unstage changes</li>
        <li>View diffs inline</li>
        <li>Write commit messages and commit</li>
        <li>Push / pull from remote</li>
        <li>View branch information</li>
        <li>Inspect graph, stash, worktree, and conflict surfaces as they mature</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Diff Viewer</h2>
    <p>
        Click any changed file to open the diff viewer, showing side-by-side
        comparison of the current file vs. the last commit.
    </p>

    <h2>Git History View</h2>
    <p>
        Axon includes a full Git history editor view showing commit logs, author
        information, and file changes per commit.
    </p>

    <figure>
        <img src="/media/screenshots/axon-screenshot-04.png" alt="Axon Git history view with a selected commit and file diff" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>The history view shows commit metadata and changed files beside the diff so you can inspect how a change was made.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Git Commands</h2>
    <p>
        Most Git operations are also available from the integrated terminal if
        you prefer the command line.
    </p>

    <h2>Agent-assisted commits</h2>
    <p>
        Axon Agent can draft commit messages from the current Git diff. The
        terminal command <code>axon commit</code> reads staged changes, streams
        a message draft, and asks before running <code>git commit</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Still being improved</h2>
    <p>
        Active Git work includes richer conflict resolution, safer stash flows,
        cherry-pick and rebase flows, fuller worktree management, and later
        pull-request review integration.
    </p>
</DocsLayout>
